      "text": "Speculative Decoding",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Speculative Decoding",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Tyju6j4Zbvt1orwUHDanU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -955.9939997373875,
      "y": 6897.081291354444,
      "width": 934.6541748046875,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "Yc56Lr441omfA7yWYxtXn",
        "YY_UPpZaPGK6cuFbGegp4",
        "almf3daoHx5C6HjsH5xwC"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2066327764,
      "version": 1125,
      "versionNonce": 157036116,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789249257934,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Speculative decoding (SD) (Leviathan et al., 2023) is a method for accelerating the inference\nof autoregressive transformer models by employing a faster assistant model. The assistant\nmodel generates a sequence of candidate tokens, all of which are verified by the main model in\na single forward pass. By generating with the faster assistant model and only performing\nvalidation forward passes with the main model, the decoding process is sped-up significantly.\nThe i-th candidate token from the assistant model ŷi is only kept if all previous candidate\ntokens ŷ<i match the validation tokens predicted by the main model. Consequently, speculative\ndecoding ensures that the generated output exactly matches the sequence of tokens that\nwould be generated by the main model, making it a natural replacement for existing inference\npipelines that use the main model.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Speculative decoding (SD) (Leviathan et al., 2023) is a method for accelerating the inference of autoregressive transformer models by employing a faster assistant model. The assistant model generates a sequence of candidate tokens, all of which are verified by the main model in a single forward pass. By generating with the faster assistant model and only performing validation forward passes with the main model, the decoding process is sped-up significantly. The i-th candidate token from the assistant model ŷi is only kept if all previous candidate tokens ŷ<i match the validation tokens predicted by the main model. Consequently, speculative decoding ensures that the generated output exactly matches the sequence of tokens that would be generated by the main model, making it a natural replacement for existing inference pipelines that use the main model.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
